Not super happy about our options to "get at" the `DefaultPartHttpMessageReader`. 

I chose to use an auto-configured customizer rather than insert a specific `Consumer<Object>` in [WebFluxAutoConfiguration.java](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/blob/main/spring-boot-project/spring-boot-autoconfigure/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/autoconfigure/web/reactive/WebFluxAutoConfiguration.java#L182) such as :
```java
		@Override
		public void configureHttpMessageCodecs(ServerCodecConfigurer configurer) {
             configurer.defaultCodecs().configureDefaultCodec((codec) -> { ... });
			this.codecCustomizers.orderedStream().forEach((customizer) -> customizer.customize(configurer));
		}
```
Seemed less intrusive and more auto-configed-like.

